{"seq":15,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/hermes-haiku-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r2","wall_ts":"2026-10-27T01:05:59.636Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"b8eb2ced0c304ed5bab8527583228c88cd71b8708b861aa15ba6f93614f3672d","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"#coastal-team","text":"@bettina.kroll here is the list for Kwame's account review. Pellow Home Living is left out. Sources are the Coastal channels and Moss's Coastal digests and cheat sheet, plus your 2025-12-08 cutover recap.\n\nPellucid Harbor Logistics (PHL)\n- Ticket #4419: Yard_Dwell_Summary report times out when filtered by container length (cheat sheet, open). Conflict: Moss's 2025-11-02 digest files #4419 under Puget Sound Operations for barge slip 7 schedule sync. Someone should confirm which account owns #4419.\n- Ticket PD-8841: chassis pool holds on double-booked gates, Gate 4B (your 2025-12-08 recap; Hector at the Beaumont barge slip).\n- Untracked: CSV import bug on the Berth 2 yard map (recap, no ticket number).\n- Untracked: Gate 4B printer mapping (recap, no ticket number).\n- Untracked: chassis pool validation at Gate 4 during shift change is the main friction point (cheat sheet, no ticket number).\n\nDriftmoor Marine Freight (DMF)\n- Feature request #882: bulk-clear button for departed barges (cheat sheet).\n- Tide-table import macro failed on Terminal B; engineering gave a manual CSV patch for the night dispatcher (cheat sheet, no ticket number).\n- Patched manifest CSV requested before the 06:00 shift (2025-11-02 digest, no ticket number; check whether it was delivered).\n\nI did not find any other tickets or feature requests for these two accounts in the Coastal channels or the Coastal files I can read."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124"}}
